## Update man pages

Make sure no calls to `compileNimble` are in any examples that are not wrapped in a `\dontrun`; in the past, these calls have  caused installation failure on Solaris and big headaches with CRAN. It looks like Solaris may no longer be part of the CRAN checking, but best to avoid compilation for fear of similar issues.

First make sure there is`nimble/R/config.R`. Copy over from another location if needed, but it should not be tracked in the GitHub repository per Duncan Temple Lang instructions. (Or do in separate copy of repository: `make configure; cd nimble; ./configure`. Note that if you do this, the configure step will have an error in building `libnimble.a` and that a bunch of files will be created in `src` that should not be in the repository (only `*.in` and `nimble.cpp` belong).)

`config.R` should be this:
```
NeedMakevarsFile = TRUE
UseLibraryMakevars = TRUE
.NimbleUseRegistration = TRUE
```

Check if there are any new undocumented functions or objects that need to be exported. If so, add these to the appropriate places in `prep_pkg.R`.

At this point, I often build and install nimble first, though I don't know it is strictly necessary before running `make man`.

Run `make man`, which will invoke `prep_pkg.R`.

(Note that an error: "section title spans multiple lines" will occur in roxygenization if any "@section" line does not have a ":" at the end of the line.)

That creates man pages and updates `NAMESPACE`.

`git add` any new .Rd files that are created in `nimble/man`.

