## Check reverse dependencies

CRAN does this, so we need to be careful that nimble updates don't break any dependent packages. Note that this takes a while.

Note that as of version 0.11.0 I was having trouble getting this to work unless I manually download the source tarballs of the dependent packages, as the default now seems to be to download the non-source Linux binary packages. It's best to download them to `nimble/packages/rev_deps` as otherwise some built objects populate `nimble/packages/nimble` and we don't want those accidentally committed to the repo.

From `nimble/packages/rev_deps`, with the current nimble .tar.gz in that directory (and having re-downloaded the dependencies' .tar.gz files when dependencies' versions have changed), do:

```
out <- tools::check_packages_in_dir('.', reverse = list())
summary(out)
```

You may also want/need to look in the `<package>.Rcheck` directory for the dependent packages, examining the `00check.log` (particularly) and `00install.out` (and perhaps `<package>-Ex.Rout`) to make sure everything is ok

One can also do this to see if anything has changed relative to current nimble and previous dependencies' versions:

```
tools::check_packages_in_dir_changes('.', old = '../rev_deps_previous_version')
```

Copy `rev_deps` to `rev_deps_previous_version` for the next time around.

Possibly also (manually) run R CMD check and tests for `nimbleSMC`, `nimbleHMC`, `nimbleQuad`, particularly if we are updating those packages in conjunction.



